---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout
	title="Discriminant & Nature of Roots | Quadratic Equations | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Learn how to find the nature of roots using the discriminant D = b² - 4ac for Class 10 Mathematics."
>
	<main class="lesson-page">
		<div class="lesson-container">
			<a href="/quadratic-equations" class="back-link">
				<span class="back-arrow">←</span>
				<span>Back to Quadratic Equations</span>
			</a>

			<!-- LESSON HEADER -->
			<section class="lesson-header">
				<div class="lesson-number">05</div>
				<div class="lesson-header-copy">
					<div class="lesson-label">LESSON 05 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS</div>
					<h1>Discriminant & <span>Nature of Roots</span></h1>
					<p>
						Determine the nature of roots of ax² + bx + c = 0 without solving the equation by using the discriminant D = b² - 4ac.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CONTENT LAYOUT -->
			<section class="content-layout">
				<article class="lesson-content">

					<!-- 01 · THE DISCRIMINANT -->
					<div class="topic-label">01 · THE DISCRIMINANT</div>
					<h2>What is the Discriminant (D)?</h2>
					<p>
						In the quadratic formula <em>x = (-b ± √(b² - 4ac)) / (2a)</em>, the expression under the square root sign <strong>b² - 4ac</strong> is called the <strong>Discriminant</strong>, denoted by <strong>D</strong>.
					</p>

					<div class="formula-box">
						<strong>D = b² - 4ac</strong>
						<span>The value of D determines whether the equation has real, equal, or no real roots!</span>
					</div>

					<!-- 02 · THREE CONDITIONS FOR NATURE OF ROOTS -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">02 · THREE CONDITIONS</div>
					<h2>The 3 Cases for Nature of Roots</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>If D &gt; 0 (Positive)</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px; font-weight:500;">Two distinct real roots exist: <em>x = (-b ± √D) / 2a</em></span>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>If D = 0 (Zero)</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px; font-weight:500;">Two equal real roots exist: <em>x = -b / 2a</em></span>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>If D &lt; 0 (Negative)</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px; font-weight:500;">No real roots exist (square root of negative number is not real).</span>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 03 · SOLVED EXAMPLES -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">03 · SOLVED EXAMPLES</div>
					<h2>Determining Nature of Roots</h2>

					<!-- Example 1 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 1</span>
							<h3>Find the discriminant of 2x² - 4x + 3 = 0 and state the nature of its roots</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p><strong>Step 1: Identify coefficients</strong>: a = 2, b = -4, c = 3.</p>
							<p><strong>Step 2: Calculate D = b² - 4ac</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								D = (-4)² - 4(2)(3) = 16 - 24 = <strong>-8</strong>
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:12px;">Since D = -8 &lt; 0, <strong>the given equation has NO real roots</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Example 2 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 2</span>
							<h3>Find the value of k if 2x² + kx + 3 = 0 has two equal real roots</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p><strong>Step 1: Condition for equal roots</strong> is <strong>D = 0</strong>.</p>
							<p>Here, a = 2, b = k, c = 3.</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								b² - 4ac = 0<br/>
								k² - 4(2)(3) = 0<br/>
								k² - 24 = 0 ⟹ k² = 24<br/>
								<strong>k = ± √24 = ± 2√6</strong>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 04 · QUICK SUMMARY -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">04 · QUICK SUMMARY</div>
					<h2>Summary Table</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>D &gt; 0</span>
							<p><strong>Two distinct real roots</strong></p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>D = 0</span>
							<p><strong>Two equal real roots</strong></p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>D &lt; 0</span>
							<p><strong>No real roots</strong></p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- LESSON NAVIGATION -->
					<div class="lesson-navigation">
						<a href="/quadratic-equations/quadratic-formula" class="previous-lesson">
							<span>←</span>
							<div>
								<small>PREVIOUS LESSON</small>
								<strong>The Quadratic Formula</strong>
							</div>
						</a>

						<a href="/quadratic-equations/pyqs" class="next-lesson">
							<div>
								<small>NEXT LESSON</small>
								<strong>Previous Year PYQs</strong>
							</div>
							<span>→</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- SIDEBAR -->
				<aside class="lesson-sidebar">
					<div class="sidebar-card">
						<div class="sidebar-title">QUADRATIC EQUATIONS</div>
						<div class="progress-text">Lesson 05 of 06</div>
						<div class="progress-bar">
							<div style="width: 83.3%;"></div>
						</div>

						<div class="sidebar-lessons">
							<a href="/quadratic-equations/introduction" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>01</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Introduction</strong>
									<small>Standard form & basics</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/quadratic-equations/factorisation" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>02</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Factorisation Method</strong>
									<small>Splitting the middle term</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/quadratic-equations/completing-the-square" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>03</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Completing the Square</strong>
									<small>Perfect square method</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/quadratic-equations/quadratic-formula" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>04</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Quadratic Formula</strong>
									<small>Formula & solutions</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/quadratic-equations/nature-of-roots" class="sidebar-lesson active">
								<span>05</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Nature of Roots</strong>
									<small>Discriminant D = b² - 4ac</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/quadratic-equations/pyqs" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>06</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Previous Year PYQs</strong>
									<small>CBSE 2020-2024 practice set</small>
								</div>
							</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</section>
		</div>
	</main>

